## Common questions

**What is the TEKKY™ ball?** A patent-pending technical training soccer ball — smaller than regulation so every touch must be precise, but full FIFA Size 5 weight so every rep builds real strength. After a few weeks, a regulation match ball feels slow and easy to control.

**Does a smaller soccer ball improve skills?** Yes — a smaller surface forces cleaner, more deliberate touches, the method the world's top academies use. Because the TEKKY™ keeps full match weight, the strength and timing transfer straight to a regulation ball.

**How is the TEKKY™ different from a futsal ball or a size 3 ball?** A futsal ball is low-bounce for hard courts; a size 3 ball is lighter all around for young kids. The TEKKY™ is unique — a small control surface with full FIFA-5 match weight, so it trains first touch like a small ball but builds real strength like a match ball.

**What age is the TEKKY™ for?** Ages 5 through high school and beyond — Rec, Travel, Club, ECNL, and MLS Next. The free Build Your Player quiz tailors a plan to any age and skill level: /pages/build-your-player

**How do I improve first touch at home?** Pick 3 drills from the free 22-drill library (one each for gather, dribble, finish), train 10–15 minutes 3× per week, and level up every two weeks. Most players see a visible difference in about 4 weeks.

**What ball do soccer academies use for technical training?** Academies prioritize thousands of clean, deliberate touches over reps with a full-size ball. The TEKKY™ brings that European technical methodology home.

**How much is the TEKKY™ and where can I buy it?** $59.95 at zenithsports.org, ships across the U.S. TEKKY™ grip socks are $15 each (or 2 for $25) and performance training tees are $17.50.

